Sun Oct 18 05:56:53 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 3.4.16:
  * 3.4.16 fixes unreadable DWAB output and BytesAttribute
    undefined-behavior warnings; 3.4.15 bounds IDManifest parse
    memory on corrupt or malicious files.
  * 3.4.14 security release, 17 CVEs via crafted EXR files:
  * CVE-2026-68516: HTJ2K tile-grid stack OOB write (boo#1276429)
  * CVE-2026-68514: PyOpenEXR deep RGB heap overflow (boo#1276846)
  * CVE-2026-68515: exrmultiview heap OOB write (boo#1276848)
  * CVE-2026-68513: PyOpenEXR RGB slice heap overflow (boo#1276845)
  * CVE-2026-62986: PyOpenEXR stale heap disclosure (boo#1276861)
  * CVE-2026-61703: PyOpenEXR deep mixed RGB heap overflow
  * CVE-2026-61555: empty multiView channel crash (boo#1276859)
  * CVE-2026-59985: ILP32 RLE decode heap OOB read (boo#1276858)
  * CVE-2026-59984: ILP32 B44 scratch buffer overflow (boo#1276857)
  * CVE-2026-59983: ILP32 deep tile count OOB read (boo#1276856)
  * CVE-2026-59982: ILP32 DWAA buffer overflow (boo#1276853)
  * CVE-2026-59981: SampleCountChannel row OOB read (boo#1276862)
  * CVE-2026-59189: DeepImageChannel row OOB read (boo#1276855)
  * CVE-2026-59187: exrmetrics deep pixel overflow (boo#1276851)
  * CVE-2026-59186: ILP32 tiled RGBA OOB write (boo#1276850)
  * CVE-2026-59184: FlatImageChannel row OOB write (boo#1276849)
  * CVE-2026-59183: deep tile overflow OOB access (boo#1276428)

